WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.910
Now, next question, will Republicans consider
Biden illegitimate for four years?

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:11.889
Yeah, I think that this is sort of a good
question to be asking the questions about

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:14.120
will Biden really be sworn in?

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.709
Seem like a waste of time.

00:00:15.709 --> 00:00:21.439
The questions about can Donald Trump really
do this, that that that that, you know, all

00:00:21.439 --> 00:00:25.540
of these six, seven, eight different things
that he's floated or others have floated as

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.539
ways to maybe steal the election.

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:32.680
We mentioned some of them earlier lawsuits
or seizing voting machines, having governors

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:33.870
send different electors.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.380
All that's none of that stuff is going to
happen.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:41.490
I think the right question is how corrosive
is Donald Trump insisting on this stuff to

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:49.760
democracy and in particular, the way in which
Donald Trump maybe never conceding and insisting

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:56.760
he actually won, will affect the Republican
Party through Joe Biden's first two years

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:57.760
and.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.190
Four years in the Oval Office now, I think
there's two sides of it.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:03.050
One is how will it affect Republican officials?

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.530
And the second part is how will it affect
Republican voters?

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.030
Let's do voters first, because I think that
one's really easy.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:13.399
I think it's very clear at this point that
the combination of Trump insisting it was

00:01:13.399 --> 00:01:14.950
I mean, just listen to the voicemails I get.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:23.109
People are convinced, Trump insisting he really
won combined with Newsmax and 081 and, you

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:28.219
know, of the different the different hosts
and characters that have been insisting Trump

00:01:28.219 --> 00:01:30.000
actually won.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.579
That will leave a significant portion of the
75 million who voted for Trump, believing

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:41.649
Joe Biden is an illegitimate president for
the duration of Joe Biden's term.

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:42.670
There's no question about that.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:44.009
One is easy for me.

00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:45.840
The voters have been affected.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.900
Many believe Trump one, etc..

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.060
Full stop.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:53.060
The more interesting question in terms of
Biden's governance, because Biden can't really

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:57.140
do anything about millions of Republicans
thinking he's an illegitimate president.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:02.709
The real question is about Biden's governance
and will Republican elected officials, Republicans

00:02:02.709 --> 00:02:07.399
in the Senate, Republicans in the House of
Representatives and Republican governors around

00:02:07.399 --> 00:02:15.470
the country, will they in some way resist
working with Biden in any way, specifically

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:20.200
by by failing him to recognize failing to
recognize him as a legitimate president?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:25.260
And I think it comes down to how visible Trump
will be after January 20th if we've already

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:29.840
seen more and more Republicans just say Biden
one.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.861
Mitch McConnell even congratulated Biden last
week.

00:02:31.861 --> 00:02:32.861
We covered that.

00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:34.530
Trump was very triggered by it.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:40.430
If Donald Trump just sort of evaporates politically,
fades away on January 20th or before or slightly

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:45.330
after, I think you will see the vast majority
of Republicans go back to dealing with Joe

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:49.270
Biden the way they dealt with Barack Obama,
which is there will be some who said Barack

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.800
Obama wasn't really born here and isn't a
legitimate president.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:57.030
But for the most part, they did the normal
Republican things obstruct, pretend to be

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.720
worried about the debt and deficit, call things
government takeovers.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:04.870
Any time the Democratic president wants to
do something, I think that's what you will

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.030
see most Republicans go back to you.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:13.530
Now, the difference is there are some really
wacky Congress people elect ready to be sworn

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:17.920
in the House of Representatives in just days.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.350
And I think that regardless of what Trump
does, there's there's Kuhnen people who are

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.350
entering Congress.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.530
You know, you have to understand the impact
of that.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:31.970
I think they will continue to say they're
absolutely wacky stuff for for the duration

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.290
of their terms.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:39.530
And hopefully they will be so ostracized by
left and right that they will lose in twenty,

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.530
twenty two.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.720
That would be the hope.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:42.720
It may not happen.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.300
We may see more kuhnen stuff in twenty, twenty
two.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.260
I just don't know yet.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:48.980
So that that's basically the lay of the land.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:56.550
I think that what Trump has done has irreversibly
put millions of his supporters in the mindset

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:58.010
that Biden is not legitimate.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.440
I'm hearing from them in my voicemail every
single week.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:04.500
But the real question in terms of Biden for
governance is how will Republican senators

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.510
and members of Congress consider him?

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.750
And I think for the most part, they will see
him as the legitimate president.

